  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a connected graph with NNN vertices (numbered 111 through NNN) and N−1N - 1N−1 bidirectional edges. Also, you are given a sequence K1,K2,…,KNK_1, K_2, \\ldots, K_NK1​,K2​,…,KN​.\n\nLet's denote the distance between vertices uuu and vvv by d(u,v)d(u, v)d(u,v). Next, for each valid iii, let's define DiD_iDi​ as the maximum integer such that there are at least KiK_iKi​ vertices vvv with d(i,v)&gt;Did(i, v) \\gt D_id(i,v)&gt;Di​. (It can be proven that such integers exist for the given constraints.)\n\nYour task is to find the values of D1,D2,…,DND_1, D_2, \\ldots, D_ND1​,D2​,…,DN​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ki≤N−11 \\le K_i \\le N - 11≤Ki​≤N−1 for each valid iii",
      "1≤u,v≤N1 \\le u, v \\le N1≤u,v≤N",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points):** 1≤N≤1031 \\le N \\le 10^31≤N≤103"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers K1,K2,…,KNK_1, K_2, \\ldots, K_NK1​,K2​,…,KN​.\nEach of the next N−1N - 1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integeres uuu and vvv denoting that vertices uuu and vvv are connected by an edge.",
    "outputFormat": "Print a single line containing NNN space-separated integers D1,D2,…,DND_1, D_2, \\ldots, D_ND1​,D2​,…,DN​.",
